# Agent Documentation Rule

## Source of Truth

Canonical Agent behavior specs live in `docs/agent/`:

| Document | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `AGENT_PLAYBOOK.md` | Product constitution |
| `PRIVACY_CONSTITUTION.md` | Hard privacy invariants |
| `TOOL_POLICY.md` | Approved/forbidden tools |
| `COMMERCIAL_LANGUAGE.md` | Voice and Hebrew UX |
| `GOLDEN_CONVERSATIONS.md` | Regression scenarios G-01–G-40 |
| `CHANGELOG.md` | Product-level Agent change log |
| `GAP_ANALYSIS_*.md` | Implementation gap tracking |

If code and documentation disagree: **privacy and hard product invariants win** — fix the discrepancy immediately.

## Required on Every Agent Behavior Change

Any change affecting Agent authority, privacy, tool access, retrieval strategy, commercial language, confirmation rules, conversation state, or Golden Conversations **must** in the same commit:

1. Update the relevant `docs/agent/*` document
2. Update or add a Golden Conversation in `GOLDEN_CONVERSATIONS.md`
3. Add/update regression tests where feasible (`tests/assistant-v2.test.ts` or eval suite)
4. Update `docs/agent/CHANGELOG.md`

## Do Not

- Silently change Agent behavior without doc updates
- Introduce forbidden network tools (see `TOOL_POLICY.md` §7)
- Autonomously express Interest or bypass Reveal
- Default to unconditional tool fan-out on every turn

## Before Implementing Agent 2.3+

Read `docs/agent/GAP_ANALYSIS_2.2.md` and classify impact against Golden Conversations.
